The Guardian of Giving said to the Guardian of Keeping: "Let us share our waters. Send some of yours to my valley, and I shall return it threefold from the mountain springs."

The Guardian of Keeping was suspicious. "How do I know you will return what you promise?"

"You must trust," said the Guardian of Giving. "But I cannot force you."

The first year, Keeping sent only a trickle. Giving returned three times that amount, as promised. The second year, Keeping sent a little more. Again, Giving multiplied and returned it faithfully.

By the third year, Keeping grew confident and sent half their water. But that winter, an earthquake struck, and the mountain springs ran dry. Giving had nothing to return.

Keeping raged: "Betrayer!" and withheld all water forever after.

But Giving wept: "I wanted to return it. The mountain failed us both."

The valleys below both rivers became deserts.

